Notebook[{
Cell["HypergraphRule", "ObjectName",ExpressionUUID->"0f2c5aa4-7e7c-d44d-8458-cff7d02c5ae4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"HypergraphRule", "[", 
    RowBox[{"input", ",", " ", "output"}], "]"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"a098d3e1-e483-4c49-a106-acbdc0d8b80c"],
 " ",
 "represents the rewrite rule taking the hypergraph input to the hypergraph \
output."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"1ae00328-556a-f64f-8259-5e2a619470c7"],

Cell["Details and Options", "NotesSection",ExpressionUUID->"2637d4a7-a061-9746-9203-ecafafb60114"],

Cell["\<\
Either side may be given as anything Hypergraph accepts, and is converted; a \
side that is not a hypergraph gives HypergraphRule::hg.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"eee38408-2f19-1a4c-832c-005652d5651b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"rule", "[", "hg", "]"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"a8ad0cd4-8310-184f-8af4-6311bcf2fc22"],
 " applies the rule, giving one event for every way the input matches. See ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["HypergraphRuleApply", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"8b3e2df1-7e68-4244-ad66-5b81a5ba6c70"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"58a04b01-9781-e44f-b766-eafe68b99789"],

Cell["\<\
A vertex of the input that the output keeps is carried through the rewrite; \
one the output introduces is created fresh; one the output drops is \
destroyed. \"SharedVertices\", \"NewVertices\" and \"DeletedVertices\" report \
the three groups, read off the two sides by vertex identifier.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"c23533fb-a578-8643-9091-e05412694206"],

Cell["\<\
Vertices correspond between the two sides by identifier, so the same name on \
both sides means the same vertex, and a name on the output alone means a new \
one.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"da0456bf-c55b-6b47-8561-384d08562fa3"],

Cell["\<\
The shape follows the reference paclet this package grew out of, so that \
rules written for that one read the same here.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"7b62e441-e4d0-ba40-a130-00bc19ed016e"],

Cell["Examples", "PrimaryExamplesSection",ExpressionUUID->"7a3be8fd-d709-5343-b6ee-289542607625"],

Cell["\<\
Subdividing an edge: the two endpoints are kept, a third vertex is new.\
\>", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"9bc08ef7-b891-ac4a-90cf-072f0d202c03"],

Cell["sub = HypergraphRule[{{1, 2}}, {{1, 3}, {3, 2}}]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"c675ffdb-46a4-e447-9169-8ac5dc7deca7"],

